; Hyperpose branches that enter many relations at once: each relation's
; program is compiled into the session's cache from a worker thread, while the
; other branches read and grow it.  The cache is changed under its lock, and a
; program leaves it retained, so the answers are the branches' and the session
; ends cleanly.  The answer bags are SWI-PeTTa's.

